-03T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 2.56, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 8.12, "poll_sd": 4.9, "poll_weight": 0.54, "fundamentals": {"margin": -0.35, "lean": -4.5, "environment": 4.15, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 4.5, "sigma_race": 5.2, "sigma_total": 5.66, "baseline_margin": 5.58, "analyst_adjustment": 0.42, "key_factors": ["Sand leads in every poll taken since June, averaging about 7 points, with large nonpartisan surveys showing double-digit margins", "Open seat in a midterm environment that favors the party out of power, with Reynolds retiring and no incumbent advantage on either side", "Betting markets price Sand above 80 percent and most race raters call the race a Democratic lean or better", "Iowa's Republican lean and GOP efforts to motivate a frustrated base keep the race from reaching safe territory"], "rationale": "Polls consistently show Sand ahead by three to twelve points, raters mostly call the race a Democratic lean, and markets price his chances above 80 percent, supporting a clear Democratic edge. Iowa's Republican-leaning electorate and the volatility of an open-seat race temper the margin to Likely Democratic rather than stronger.", "watch": "Watch whether Republican base mobilization and attacks portraying Sand as wealthy and out of touch narrow the polling gap among rural voters in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Kim Reynolds (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's governor race is an open contest after Republican Kim Reynolds chose not to run again, pitting Democrat Rob Sand against Republican Zach Lahn, with independent Sondra Wilson also on the ballot. Every poll since June has shown Sand ahead, with recent surveys from Marist and YouGov giving him double-digit leads while Republican-sponsored polls show narrower four-point margins. Race raters mostly call it a Democratic lean, ranging from Tossup to Likely Democratic, and betting markets put Sand's chances above 80 percent.\n\nThe state's Republican lean puts a ceiling on the Democratic edge. Republicans are working to motivate a frustrated base, and opinion pieces portray Sand as wealthy and out of touch, while his town-hall-heavy campaign seeks support beyond the Democratic base. The consistent polling lead, favorable midterm environment, and Sand's statewide profile point to a Democratic advantage in this open-seat race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8753, "margin": 5.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8859, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8669, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8657, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8472, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8297, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8592, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8769, "margin": 6.0}]}